<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Oneida Nation</h1><p class="st-meta">1450 CE – present (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The People of the Standing Stone, one of the five founding nations of the Iroquois Confederacy, and the main Haudenosaunee ally of the Americans in the Revolution.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Oneida took shape as a nation in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oneida-lake">Oneida Lake</a> and Oneida <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a>, their name recalling a boulder that marked their principal settlement. Around the mid-15th century, according to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/iroquois-confederacy">Haudenosaunee</a> tradition, they joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mohawk-nation">Mohawk</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/onondaga-nation">Onondaga</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cayuga-nation">Cayuga</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/seneca-nation">Seneca</a> in accepting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-law-of-peace">Great Law of Peace</a>, forming the Iroquois <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/confederate-states-of-america">Confederacy</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Like the other member nations, the Oneida were organised in clans, with women owning the longhouses and fields and clan mothers selecting the chiefs who represented the nation, nine of them, at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-council-qing">Grand Council</a>. Villages farmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maize">maize</a>, beans and squash and traded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">furs</a>. In council they sat with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cayuga-nation">Cayuga</a> as the younger brothers. Influenced by the Presbyterian missionary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-kirkland">Samuel Kirkland</a>, many converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> in the 18th century.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolution">American Revolution</a> the Oneida fought for the Americans at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-oriskany">Oriskany</a> and sent corn to Valley Forge, yet lost most of their land through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> State treaties. Many moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wisconsin">Wisconsin</a> in the 1820s and to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ontario">Ontario</a> in 1840. Today there are Oneida nations in New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york-maine">York</a>, Wisconsin and Ontario.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 1450 CE – present (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">North America and Oceania</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:88.56%;width:11.44%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1450 CE – present (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Skenandoah, Han Yerry</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Haudenosaunee traditional religion, Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Oneida</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a>, <a href="/countries/canada">Canada</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Onyota'a:ka, Oneida</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1738&amp;focus=oneida-nation" aria-label="Oneida Nation on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2572 604 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Oneida Nation lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><pat